<body>
  <h1>THEXRA ENTERPRISE SOLUTION BRIEF</h1>
  <p><strong>Date:</strong> 06/10/2026 | <strong>Status:</strong> Approved Architecture Brief</p>
  
  <h2>1. Client Problem Statement</h2>
  <p>Remote engineering students lack access to dangerous and expensive high-voltage electrical engineering lab equipment, preventing hands-on practical skill acquisition.</p>
  <p><strong>Target Users:</strong> Remote electrical engineering undergraduate students, laboratory instructors, and academic curriculum administrators.</p>

  <h2>2. AI Rationale & Analysis</h2>
  <p><em>"Augmented reality allows engineering students to safely visualize and interact with complex high-voltage equipment anywhere without physical safety risks or equipment procurement costs. THEXRA Make provides an intuitive authoring platform for faculty to rapidly digitize complex laboratory protocols into guided spatial learning modules."</em></p>
  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong> Requires compatible mobile devices or smart tablets for spatial tracking, Limited tactile feedback compared to physical electrical components, Dependent on stable internet connectivity for initial cloud asset streaming</p>

<h2>3. Proposed Solution Concept</h2>
<p>An interactive spatial laboratory application that allows remote engineering students to simulate high-voltage circuitry, switchgear operations, and electrical safety procedures in augmented reality on personal mobile and tablet devices.</p>


  <h2>Detailed Implementation Roadmap (7 Stages)</h2>
  
    <ol style="margin: 0; padding-left: 16px; color: #334155; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.3;">
      <li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Discovery</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(1 week):</span>Laboratory curriculum mapping document • CAD asset readiness audit report</li><li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Design</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(1.5 weeks):</span>3D circuit interaction design guide • User experience wireframes for mobile AR</li><li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Prototype</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(1.5 weeks):</span>Single interactive switchgear prototype • Safety validation test run</li><li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Development</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(3 weeks):</span>Full high-voltage lab module suite • LMS grading integration module</li><li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Testing</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(1.5 weeks):</span>Multi-device QA matrix report • Student usability evaluation summary</li><li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Deployment</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(1.5 weeks):</span>Live app deployment on THEXRA View • Faculty administration onboarding package</li><li style="margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #0284C7;">Support</strong> <span style="color: #64748B;">(Ongoing):</span>Curriculum content updates SLA • Monthly student telemetry platform report</li>
    </ol>
  



  <h2>Scope of Work (SOW)</h2>
  <p><strong>Project Scope:</strong> End-to-end design, creation, and deployment of interactive augmented reality high-voltage engineering laboratory exercises using THEXRA Make and THEXRA View for remote student access.</p>
  <p><strong>Features:</strong> Interactive 3D switchgear, transformer, and breaker simulation, Virtual multimeter and voltage testing probes, Lockout-Tagout (LOTO) safety procedure verification, Step-by-step guided and test-mode evaluations, Automatic student error flagging and scoring export</p>
  <p><strong>Deliverables:</strong> 3 interactive high-voltage laboratory simulation modules, THEXRA Make instructional authoring templates, Student mobile AR application deployment package, Instructor grading and telemetry integration documentation</p>
  <p><strong>Hardware:</strong> Client-provided iOS and Android tablets or smartphones running ARCore/ARKit</p>
  <p><strong>Software:</strong> THEXRA Make creator license, THEXRA View cross-platform student viewer application, Cloud telemetry and LMS synchronization connector</p>
  <p><strong>Content:</strong> Optimized 3D models of high-voltage industrial switchgear, High-fidelity electrical transformer components, Instructional spatial overlays and warning visual effects</p>
  <p><strong>Training:</strong> Interactive virtual training workshops for faculty on authoring new lab procedures in THEXRA Make and monitoring student progress dashboards.</p>
  <p><strong>Deployment:</strong> Distribution of the THEXRA View runtime app via institutional enterprise application catalogs and mobile app stores with LMS student single sign-on.</p>
  <p><strong>Support:</strong> Dedicated technical support SLA covering application bug fixes, platform updates, and content assistance for 12 months.</p>
  <p><strong>Exclusions:</strong> Physical laboratory hardware modifications, Procurement of mobile student devices or smart glasses, Custom electrical physical circuit simulation beyond programmed digital switchgear models</p>


  <div class="tech-box">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0; color:#0f172a;">4. Technology Architecture Blueprint</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14pt; font-weight:bold; color:#0f172a;">AR — THEXRA Make</p>
    
      <p><strong>1. Solution Overview:</strong> The system deploys 3D interactive high-voltage laboratory simulations authored via THEXRA Make directly to student mobile and tablet devices using THEXRA View. Students interact with photorealistic digital switchboards and transformers while telemetry data tracks safety protocol compliance back to faculty dashboards.</p>
      <p><strong>2. User Journey:</strong> Student logs into THEXRA View on their mobile device, selects the assigned high-voltage lab module, places virtual switchgear in their physical room via spatial tracking, executes step-by-step lockout/tagout and switching procedures, receives real-time validation, and the system logs their test score to the academic portal.</p>
      <p><strong>3. Hardware:</strong> Student iOS/Android tablets or smartphones with ARCore/ARKit support, Optional HTC VIVE Eagle smart glasses for hands-free lab review</p>
      <p><strong>4. Software:</strong> THEXRA Make content authoring engine, THEXRA View cross-platform runtime client, Learning Management System (LMS) LTI integration adapter</p>
      <p><strong>5. AI Components:</strong> Automated procedural mistake detection module, Real-time electrical hazard warning heuristics</p>
      <p><strong>6. XR Components:</strong> Surface-anchored 3D electrical equipment tracking, Interactive spatial switchgear and multimeter widgets, Simulated arc flash visual indicators</p>
      <p><strong>7. Backend:</strong> Cloud asset streaming repository, PostgreSQL database for student scoring and completion telemetry, Node.js API gateway with secure authentication</p>
      <p><strong>8. Dashboard:</strong> Instructor laboratory progress dashboard, Student safety compliance and procedural accuracy analytics</p>
      <p><strong>9. Data Flow:</strong> Student Device -> HTTPS Telemetry Stream -> Cloud API Gateway -> Analytics Engine -> Instructor Web Dashboard</p>
      <p><strong>Alternative Technology:</strong> Combination solution — THEXRA Suite (Remote, Make, View)</p>
    
  </div>

  <h2>5. Expected Business Outcomes & KPIs</h2>
  <p>Eliminates high-voltage physical hazards, lowers laboratory hardware capital expenditure by up to 70%, and increases remote student pass rates on procedural switchgear protocols.</p>
  <p><strong>KPI Alignment:</strong> Provide remote students with safe, interactive access to standardized high-voltage lab equipment simulations to achieve 100% curriculum completion and over 85% procedural competence.</p>

  <h2>6. Recommended Next Steps</h2>
  <p>Conduct a curriculum technical audit to catalog specific high-voltage switchgear CAD assets and operating procedures for digital conversion.</p>
